Test: String and Array Literal Whitespace
--------------------------------------

Empty string with empty brackets:
""[] = []
"" [] = []

Empty string with non-empty brackets:
""[1] =  (no space - access, out of bounds, empty)
"" [1] = [1] (space - concatenation)
""[1,2] =  (no space - access, multiple indices, empty)
"" [1,2] = [1, 2] (space - concatenation)

Non-empty string:
"hello"[1] = h (no space - access)
"hello" [1] = hello[1] (space - concatenation)
"hello"[2] = e (no space - access)
"hello" [2] = hello[2] (space - concatenation)
"test"[1,2] =  (no space - access, multiple indices, empty)
"test" [1,2] = test[1, 2] (space - concatenation)

Multi-element arrays:
"x" [1,2,3] = x[1, 2, 3] (space - concatenation)
"x"["a","b"] =  (no space - access, string indices, empty)
"x" ["a","b"] = x["a", "b"] (space - concatenation)

Variable strings:
s[1] = w (variable - access)
s [1] = w (variable with space - still access, whitespace ignored)

Number literals (always concatenation):
42[] = 42[]
42 [] = 42[]
42[1] = 42[1]
42 [1] = 42[1]

Newline as whitespace:

